## 16. Financial Calculation Rules

Centralize all financial calculations in tested utility functions.

Use reliable monetary precision. Do not rely on unrestricted JavaScript floating-point arithmetic for money.

Keep original amounts, exchange rates, commission settings, payouts, and ledger entries.

Calculate balances from recorded transactions instead of allowing users to type an arbitrary calculated balance.

Use documented adjustments and reversals for corrections. Do not silently overwrite important financial history.

Never combine AED and PKR in one total without an explicit exchange-rate conversion.

For all modules, validate that:

- Payouts do not exceed the payable balance.
- Loan repayments do not create an unexplained negative balance.
- Amanat withdrawals do not exceed the available balance.
- Completed transfers have no unexplained outstanding balance.
- Currency labels match the recorded amounts.
- Historical transactions preserve their original calculation values.

